      "message": "Okay :-) a short story, grab a coffee before reading this.\n\nIt is just handled differently in Zephyr (IMO much better). Zephyr uses [DTS system](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/build/dts/intro-syntax-structure.html) to define hardware. There are something called `nodes` - an independent parts of hardware e,g, UART module, flash chip, sensor. Each node describes a specyfic harwade type, it is specified by `compatible` string (remember that, it is very important). Each node can have some properties, depending on a hardware type, a list of properties is different. It is descirbed in [binding files](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/build/dts/bindings-syntax.html#dt-bindings-file-syntax). \n\nComming back to our case. We define a hardware type [finderprint sensor](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/dts/bindings/fingerprint/fingerprint-sensor.yaml) - with properties common for all fp sensors - width, height, etc. Then a specific fp sensor like [fpc1025](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/dts/bindings/fingerprint/fpc,fpc1025.yaml) can have some additional properties + the common ones for all sensors. In our application (AKA program/project), we define which sensor we have in our hardware - for bloonchipper it is [fpc1025](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/bloonchipper/bloonchipper.dts;l\u003d116) (it is \"inside\" spi node, because it is connected via this spi). Then, we have additional dts feature - [chosen](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/build/dts/api/api.html#chosen-nodes). It kind of points to a node that is used in system for something e.g. there is a chosen node named \"zephyr,console\", which points to a node that is used for system console. We have something like this for FP sensor. We point which sensor should be used in our project - [bloonchipper case](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/bloonchipper/bloonchipper.dts;l\u003d14). Then we can use this chosen node to get properties which we need - [x and y](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/include/fpsensor_driver.h;l\u003d29) in this case. \n\nTL;DR: This header defines are not needed in Zephyr. This info in included in hardware definition in DTS.",
